    "rationale": "Ch. 2 diagnostics: the ACF of y_t decays very slowly (still 0.90 at lag 12), which is the textbook signature of a non-stationary series, and the variance of P_t grows with its level, which calls for a variance-stabilising transform. ADF cannot reject a unit root in y_t while KPSS rejects stationarity, so d = 1. In first differences the ACF falls away within a few lags (lag 1 = 0.56, lag 3 = 0.26) and ADF rejects the unit root at conventional lag lengths (p < 0.001 at 3 and 6 lags), so the log change pi_t is the stationary series to model. The ADF evidence is weaker over 1957-79 alone, which is the 1968-82 Great Inflation regime: the sample-mean shift inflates the persistence of pi_t in that window, an effect that the ARMA terms and the deterministic part of the model absorb. The ACF of pi_t also shows a clear annual echo (lags 11-13 = 0.42, 0.46, 0.34, and Ljung-Box at lag 12 is highly significant), so a seasonal SARMA(1,1)[12] block is carried into the identification stage, while seasonal differencing (D = 1) is not imposed."
  }
